# wk memory-experiment patch: 300 MB MemoryPressureMonitor clamp
#
# docs/Urgent/HANDOFF-memory.md asks for this to be a file instead of a
# copy-paste block, so it survives past whoever currently holds it in their
# head. It is not one yet.
#
# TODO: the actual diff. It was not recoverable here -- see
# startMemorySampler.patch in this directory for why (same wiki pages, same
# 404s, same reason to capture it from a live checkout with
# `git diff > container/bin/patches/memory-pressure-300mb.patch` rather than
# reinvent it from a name).
#
# What it has to do: lower the ceiling WebCore's/WTF's MemoryPressureHandler
# uses to decide the process is under pressure, from whatever the system's
# real memory reports to a fixed 300 MB -- so a memory-charts run can compare
# how a page behaves against a small budget on hardware with much more RAM
# than the target device, without needing that device to reproduce the run.
# MemoryPressureHandler.cpp/.h (Source/WTF/wtf or Source/WebCore/platform,
# depending on branch) is where the real threshold lives; this experiment
# overrides it, most likely behind an environment variable or a debug build
# flag in whichever checkout still has this patch.
#
# Until this is a real diff, applying it is refused rather than silently
# skipped: `git apply container/bin/patches/memory-pressure-300mb.patch`
# fails on this file (it is prose, not a patch).
